<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:09:47 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>东北复活节期间，有人发现一只鲨鱼在新泽西州被洪水淹没的街道上游动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-shark-was-spotted-swimming-through-the-flooded-streets-of-new-jersey-during-the-noreaster-180989588/</link><description>该生物已被确认为光滑角鲨，这是一种在西大西洋发现的无害物种。它并不是唯一陷入风暴系统带来的混乱的动物</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-shark-was-spotted-swimming-through-the-flooded-streets-of-new-jersey-during-the-noreaster-180989588/</guid></item><item><title>英格兰备受喜爱的梧桐树在被破坏者砍倒三年后又显露出生命迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/englands-beloved-sycamore-gap-tree-is-showing-signs-of-life-three-years-after-vandals-chopped-it-down-180989591/</link><description>现在，位于英格兰北部哈德良长城附近的树桩底部周围正在长出许多绿叶芽。</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/englands-beloved-sycamore-gap-tree-is-showing-signs-of-life-three-years-after-vandals-chopped-it-down-180989591/</guid></item><item><title>当简·奥斯汀在巴斯的舞厅转一圈时，古罗马文物就藏在她的脚下。现在，考古学家终于找到了它们</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-jane-austen-took-a-turn-about-the-ballroom-in-bath-ancient-roman-artifacts-were-hiding-beneath-her-feet-now-archaeologists-have-finally-found-them-180989592/</link><description>最近在英格兰巴斯集会室进行的发掘发现了罗马时代的硬币、屋顶瓦片、陶器、玻璃器皿、沟渠网络和军用头盔的碎片</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-jane-austen-took-a-turn-about-the-ballroom-in-bath-ancient-roman-artifacts-were-hiding-beneath-her-feet-now-archaeologists-have-finally-found-them-180989592/</guid></item><item><title>核磁共振扫描可能会在大脑中出现蛛丝马迹七年前发现阿尔茨海默病的迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mri-scans-might-reveal-signs-of-alzheimers-disease-seven-years-before-a-telltale-marker-appears-in-the-brain-180989570/</link><description>并非所有研究人员都相信通过 MRI 检测到的大脑变化足以成为诊断工具。但这些发现可以帮助研究人员更好地了解驱动神经退行性疾病的机制</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:33:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mri-scans-might-reveal-signs-of-alzheimers-disease-seven-years-before-a-telltale-marker-appears-in-the-brain-180989570/</guid></item><item><title>在罗马最著名和最被忽视的别墅之一，由修女绘制的具有数百年历史的下流壁画重新出现</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-one-of-romes-most-famed-and-neglected-villas-centuries-old-risque-frescoes-painted-over-by-nuns-have-reappeared-180989585/</link><description>耗资 4000 万美元修复西尔维斯特里里瓦尔迪别墅近一年后，保护人员正在重新发现和复兴 16 世纪的艺术</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-one-of-romes-most-famed-and-neglected-villas-centuries-old-risque-frescoes-painted-over-by-nuns-have-reappeared-180989585/</guid></item><item><title>Anthropic 表示其人工智能发现了一种新的酶系统，类似于革命性的基因编辑工具 CRISPR</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/anthropic-says-its-ai-discovered-a-new-enzyme-system-that-resembles-the-revolutionary-gene-editing-tool-crispr-180989578/</link><description>该公司的专家不知道新发现的系统有什么作用，因此它在生物学中的潜在用途（如果有的话）仍不清楚。但这项工作标志着一项重大进步，因为人工智能主要是靠自己做出这一发现的</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:16:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/anthropic-says-its-ai-discovered-a-new-enzyme-system-that-resembles-the-revolutionary-gene-editing-tool-crispr-180989578/</guid></item><item><title>密尔沃基艺术博物馆刚刚将两件由被奴役的波特大卫·德雷克制作的陶瓷归还给他的后裔</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-milwaukee-art-museum-just-returned-two-ceramics-made-by-enslaved-potter-david-drake-to-his-descendants-180989586/</link><description>这两艘船，其中一艘是 1855 年签名的罐子，是德雷克家族最近重新安置的两艘船，他们的使命是获取祖先的作品</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:07:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-milwaukee-art-museum-just-returned-two-ceramics-made-by-enslaved-potter-david-drake-to-his-descendants-180989586/</guid></item><item><title>两个头比一个好：科德角发现的稀有双头海龟幼体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-heads-are-better-than-one-rare-double-headed-turtle-hatchling-discovered-on-cape-cod-180989579/</link><description>9 月 17 日，这种微小的小菜斑龟被带到野生动物中心。当时，这种生物的重量约为 5 分钱。</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:33:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-heads-are-better-than-one-rare-double-headed-turtle-hatchling-discovered-on-cape-cod-180989579/</guid></item><item><title>1884 年，一艘船在科德角附近因强风搁浅。现在，袭击东海岸的东北风暴可能已经发现了其中的一部分</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-1884-gale-force-winds-ran-a-ship-aground-near-cape-code-now-the-noreaster-lashing-the-east-coast-may-have-uncovered-part-of-it-180989583/</link><description>残骸可能属于“Warren Sawyer”号，这是一艘 140 多年前沉没的三桅货运纵帆船</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-1884-gale-force-winds-ran-a-ship-aground-near-cape-code-now-the-noreaster-lashing-the-east-coast-may-have-uncovered-part-of-it-180989583/</guid></item><item><title>几个世纪前，皇室成员打扮他们的玩偶来分享最新的时尚。了解芭比娃娃、娃娃和其他小型潮流引领者如何为设计师带来灵感</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-royals-dressed-up-their-dolls-to-share-latest-fashions-see-how-barbies-baby-dolls-and-other-tiny-trendsetters-have-inspired-designers-ever-since-180989580/</link><description>纽约市 FIT 博物馆举办的新展览展示了 170 多件物品，追溯了玩偶与时尚之间经常出人意料的关系</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:22:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-royals-dressed-up-their-dolls-to-share-latest-fashions-see-how-barbies-baby-dolls-and-other-tiny-trendsetters-have-inspired-designers-ever-since-180989580/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，由于巨大的胃和被盗的基因，这种巨大的深海不倒翁可以在没有食物的情况下生存数年</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-massive-deep-sea-roly-poly-can-go-years-without-food-thanks-to-a-huge-stomach-and-a-stolen-gene-study-suggests-180989562/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，巨型等足类动物 Bathynomus jamesi（一种类似巨大药丸虫的海底生物）的祖先在 1600 万年前从细菌中获得了 DNA 片段。该基因帮助动物减缓新陈代谢</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:53:41 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-massive-deep-sea-roly-poly-can-go-years-without-food-thanks-to-a-huge-stomach-and-a-stolen-gene-study-suggests-180989562/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家挖掘出有 2,400 年历史的学校，亚里士多德曾在这里教导亚历山大如何变得伟大</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-unearth-the-2400-year-old-school-where-aristotle-taught-alexander-to-be-great-180989581/</link><description>位于古代米耶扎的亚里士多德体育馆的最新发掘揭示了华丽的马赛克大厅，研究人员相信亚历山大大帝在这里学习了他的成长课程</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:49:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-unearth-the-2400-year-old-school-where-aristotle-taught-alexander-to-be-great-180989581/</guid></item><item><title>卫星图像显示格陵兰岛和南极洲在过去 50 年中损失了超过 12 万亿吨冰</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/satellite-images-reveal-greenland-and-antarctica-have-lost-more-than-12-trillion-tons-of-ice-over-the-past-50-years-180989567/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，大部分冰冻水已经消失，因为冰川流入海洋的速度更快，而不是因为冰盖表面融化。研究人员估计冰损失已使全球海平面上升一英寸以上</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:36:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/satellite-images-reveal-greenland-and-antarctica-have-lost-more-than-12-trillion-tons-of-ice-over-the-past-50-years-180989567/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下“火变形虫”，这是一种新发现的斑点生物，它的复杂生命能承受多少热量</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-fire-amoeba-a-newfound-blobby-organism-thats-defying-expectations-about-how-much-heat-complex-life-can-handle-180989557/</link><description>根据一项新的研究，在北加州拉森火山国家公园发现的新描述的物种仍然可以在 145 华氏度的温度下繁殖，并在 147 华氏度的温度下移动</description><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-fire-amoeba-a-newfound-blobby-organism-thats-defying-expectations-about-how-much-heat-complex-life-can-handle-180989557/</guid></item><item><title>在图坦卡蒙国王陵墓之外发现了神秘的“异常现象”。它们可能是通往失踪已久的纳芙蒂蒂王后遗骸的秘密通道吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysterious-anomalies-have-been-detected-beyond-king-tuts-tomb-could-they-be-secret-passageways-leading-to-the-long-lost-remains-of-queen-nefertiti-180989576/</link><description>地球物理调查为埃及法老被埋葬在现有墓葬群的外室的理论提供了新的证据。研究人员正试图获得批准自行调查</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:08:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysterious-anomalies-have-been-detected-beyond-king-tuts-tomb-could-they-be-secret-passageways-leading-to-the-long-lost-remains-of-queen-nefertiti-180989576/</guid></item><item><title>首次发现海龟在美国西海岸筑巢。科学家称“超级”厄尔尼诺现象可能将他们带到那里</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-sea-turtles-were-spotted-nesting-on-the-us-west-coast-scientists-say-the-super-el-nino-could-have-brought-them-there-180989574/</link><description>九月份，人们发现两只橄榄丽龟在南加州的海滩上产卵。在太平洋，这些爬行动物通常在更南的地方筑巢，通常在墨西哥、尼加拉瓜、哥斯达黎加和巴拿马</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:24:20 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-sea-turtles-were-spotted-nesting-on-the-us-west-coast-scientists-say-the-super-el-nino-could-have-brought-them-there-180989574/</guid></item><item><title>希特勒与他同父异母的侄女有着密切而神秘的关系。新研究表明他谋杀她的不在场证明可能站不住脚</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hitler-had-an-intense-mysterious-relationship-with-his-half-niece-new-research-suggests-his-alibi-for-her-murder-might-not-hold-up-180989572/</link><description>最近发现的有关吉莉·劳巴尔死亡时间的文件对这位纳粹领导人的不在场证据提出了新的怀疑，近一个世纪以来，该证据一直被认为是相当合理的</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:07:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hitler-had-an-intense-mysterious-relationship-with-his-half-niece-new-research-suggests-his-alibi-for-her-murder-might-not-hold-up-180989572/</guid></item><item><title>澳大利亚发现了两种新的竹节虫物种，另一种则隐藏在众目睽睽之下</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-new-stick-insect-species-have-been-discovered-in-australiaand-another-one-was-hiding-in-plain-sight-180989575/</link><description>新发现强调，即使在有大量观测的地区，科学家们对于昆虫多样性还有很多需要了解的地方</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:03:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-new-stick-insect-species-have-been-discovered-in-australiaand-another-one-was-hiding-in-plain-sight-180989575/</guid></item><item><title>科学家发明了一种可消化的纸基电池，可为吞咽或植入的医疗设备供电</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-invent-a-digestible-paper-based-battery-that-can-power-swallowed-or-implanted-medical-devices-180989549/</link><description>到目前为止，该技术仅在猪身上进行了测试。如果它在人类身上取得成功，有一天它可能会成为监测您健康状况或在体内输送药物或电流的电动工具</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:37:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-invent-a-digestible-paper-based-battery-that-can-power-swallowed-or-implanted-medical-devices-180989549/</guid></item><item><title>两千多年前，朱利叶斯·凯撒征服了最终成为巴黎的定居点。考古学家可能刚刚发现它</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-thousand-years-ago-julius-caesar-conquered-the-settlement-that-eventually-became-paris-archaeologists-may-have-just-found-it-180989569/</link><description>在塞纳河西岱岛的一家医院进行挖掘时，研究人员发现了可能曾经保护过卢泰西亚（法国首都的高卢前身）的城墙的一部分</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-thousand-years-ago-julius-caesar-conquered-the-settlement-that-eventually-became-paris-archaeologists-may-have-just-found-it-180989569/</guid></item></channel></rss>